{
  "measurement": "sage kernel accuracy on REAL captured H3 activations, against a float64 reference",
  "date": "2026-08-18",
  "why": "`docs/evidence.md` withdrew every fp8-vs-fp16 accuracy ratio on 2026-08-16 and stated that this repo has no accuracy figure and must not acquire one by inference. The restoring action it named was to grade a kernel against a capture. This is that run. `h3_capture.py`'s own docstring recorded that no kernel had ever been graded against the captures it produced.",
  "method": "Sampled query rows scored against the FULL key set, so the reference is exact for the rows it covers rather than an approximation of all of them. Reference is float64: an fp32 reference and torch's fp32 SDPA sit the same distance from float64 while differing from each other by more, so fp32 cannot resolve a kernel difference this small. The harness refuses to report unless its reference tracks torch AND a deliberately 1%-wrong softmax scale is caught.",
  "produced_by": "bench/grade_sage_on_capture.py",
